# Keep the build context small + never ship local state/secrets into the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
.git
.env
.env.*
apps/api/data
# ★ .data/ is the DOCUMENT-BYTES + corpus tree (blobs/, source-docs/, uploads/,
# historical-uws.json, learned-rules.json, kicks-master-list.json) — 1.4GB locally.
# The line above does NOT cover it: `apps/api/data` and `apps/api/.data` are
# different names, so without this it was silently baked into the image.
# It belongs on the cre_docs VOLUME (fly.api.toml), which mounts at this exact path
# and SHADOWS whatever the image holds there — so anything baked here is both
# 1.4GB of dead weight AND invisible at runtime. Seed the volume instead: RUNBOOK §6.
apps/api/.data
# Defensive: the real DB is data/cre.db, so a stray *.db sitting beside package.json
# (there is a 0-byte apps/api/cre.db today) is never read — it would only ride into the
# image as dead weight.
apps/api/*.db
apps/api/*.db-shm
apps/api/*.db-wal
**/*.log
deploy/dryrun-data
.DS_Store
